WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.243
- [Joanna V.O.] This is
not your typical car race.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.350
This is a race to make cars

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.083
more like computers, and smartphones,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.200
and the best one to buy.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.970
- No, it doesn't stretch.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.470
I don't want cameras anymore.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.460
I want map.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.293
Please slow down.

00:00:21.293 --> 00:00:23.460
Please don't hit the Tesla that we rented.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.840
Are you worried about dongles?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.893
- A little bit, yeah.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:27.960
- I spent the last month

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.060
in search of the perfect EV

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.700
for me and my family.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.040
That meant testing five leading options

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.700
under $60,000 over the
course of two months.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.290
The Kia EV6,

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.970
the Hyundai Ioniq 5,

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.590
the Tesla Model Y,

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.390
the Volkswagen ID.4,

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.343
and the Ford Mustang Mach-E.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.360
After narrowing it down
to three finalists,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.680
I took the remaining three

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.570
on a road trip to this racetrack

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.550
to pick the best one.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.130
I evaluated them on four features:

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.200
Battery life; charging;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.113
infotainment; and semi-autonomous driving.

00:01:05.122 --> 00:01:07.980
And yes, I've factored in
other important stuff too,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.560
including safety, handling, and...

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.790
Why do you like this car?

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.980
- Because it farts.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.813
- Let's go!

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.310
- [Joanna V.O.] Lap one, battery life,

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:23.160
or what EV people call "range."

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.840
One of the biggest pieces of criteria

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.490
I had when selecting cars,

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.610
a range of about 300 miles.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.070
To test, I recruited two of my colleagues,

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.230
and together we drove the three cars

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.400
on the same day,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.930
under the same conditions,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.673
to the same destination.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.720
That destination, Lime Rock Racetrack

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.430
in Northern Connecticut,

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.350
130 miles north of my home

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.940
in New Jersey.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.960
Before we hit the road,

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.243
we made sure every car was charged up.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.450
- Every car has to start at 100.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.283
- [Joanna V.O.] And that all

00:01:55.283 --> 00:01:57.390
the air condition levels were the same.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.070
Each car was fairly new

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.290
with relatively low mileage.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.300
To start, Tesla took the lead

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.133
about 30 miles into the drive.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.350
- What percentage are you at

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.420
and how many miles does
it say you have left?

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.997
- [Adam] I have 94%

00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:14.190
and 278 miles.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.940
- [Joanna] I'm on 93% and 266 miles.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.530
- [Joanna V.O.] The Hyundai, however...

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.130
- [Nellie] 93%, 240 miles.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.450
- [Joanna V.O.] To be
fair, the Hyundai model

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.890
I tested was rated for around

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.260
a 260 mile range.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.093
The company says

00:02:29.093 --> 00:02:31.980
its rear wheel drive
model would've kept up.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.850
Here's how that played out

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:33.683
for the rest of

00:02:33.683 --> 00:02:35.100
the two and a half hour drive.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.470
After being on the road for 75 miles,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.480
Tesla and Ford were neck and neck,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.210
around 210 miles left on the battery.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.190
Hyundai was at 190.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.670
- [Joanna] There it is, Lime Rock Park.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.543
We did it.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.040
- [Joanna V.O.] Finally,
when we arrived at the track,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.480
both the Ford and Tesla had

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.000
around 150 miles left to go.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.740
Hyundai was still behind.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.350
Still, because all these
cars can be configured

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.210
to hit a similar range,

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.190
this lap is a...

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.153
- It's a tie.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.170
- [Joanna V.O.] Lap two charging.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.020
This is really where these
cars are like smartphones.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.160
The Tesla uses its own

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.250
proprietary charging connector and port.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.720
Apple.
- It's called Lightning.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:19.553
- [Joanna V.O.] Which it now calls

00:03:19.553 --> 00:03:21.720
the "North American charging standard."

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.730
It also has its own Tesla chargers,

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.350
which are dead simple to use

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.760
after you've set up your account

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:27.630
in the app.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.840
- And green!

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:31.800
That's it.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.720
- [Joanna V.O.] Ford,
Hyundai, and those other cars

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.300
I tested use the combined charging system,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.130
or CCS port,

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.200
which work at different charging stations

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.090
from various different companies.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.710
And I found some of those stations

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.350
to be, well, unreliable.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.700
- Please work.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.990
- [Joanna V.O.] But
even when they do work,

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.880
I found that there are some big issues

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.770
with these non-Tesla stations,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.030
which can all be illustrated

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.100
in what happened in the beautiful town

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.080
of Falls Village.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.070
- Let me tell you a story about

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.750
what happened here last night.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.860
- Do you have service?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.920
- We realized that the cars were too low

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.600
to drive all the way home.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.433
because we had used them

00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:08.270
at the track a lot.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.347
Figured, "Okay, we'll
charge 'em overnight,

00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:12.900
"even though it's gonna be slow."

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.940
We met SemaConnect,

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.190
our not very good friend.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.150
- Why would you be able

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.350
to use tap to pay?

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.290
No, you've gotta download
their proprietary app.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.840
- [Joanna V.O.] Turns out
SemaConnect was acquired by Blink,

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.690
so we had to ultimately
download another app.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.800
A Blink spokesman told me

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.240
that SemaConnect's transition

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.980
to the Blink network may have caused

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.350
an inconvenience for some users.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.910
The company also plans to add

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.310
more chargers with credit card readers.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.320
SemaConnect was a slower charger,

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.910
or a level two charger,

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.680
and it took roughly six hours

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.190
to charge the cars from 40% to 100%.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:50.490
- [Joanna] All right, guys,
take care of each other.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.930
- [Joanna V.O.] DC fast charging,

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.980
or what's sometimes referred

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.240
to as level three,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.370
can do that in under an hour.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.510
And that's exactly what I did

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:59.190
with the Tesla on the road trip.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.780
I've consistently found it easier

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.990
to find Tesla fast chargers,
called "superchargers,"

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.938
especially in remote areas.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.950
The good news, Tesla has agreed

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.000
to allow other cars

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.560
from Ford, GM, and others

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.830
to access superchargers in early 2024,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.380
and I think the winner
here is pretty clear.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.003
- The Tesla wins this round.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.980
- [Joanna V.O.] Lap three, infotainment.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.480
Both Ford and Tesla have

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.280
similarly sized tablets

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.510
that have replaced pretty much

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.240
all the buttons, knobs and dials.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.740
Okay, Ford kept this knob

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.750
and this 10.2 inch screen

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.070
above the steering wheel,

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.410
so you can easily see vital information

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.060
like how fast you're going.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.500
With the Tesla, I had to look over

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.600
to the right to see that information.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.060
Hyundai also has two
screens, like the Ford.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.380
- This display here,

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.300
this is teeny tiny compared

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.910
to the Mustang and to the Tesla.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.950
Feels like a display for ants.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.360
- [Joanna V.O.] Of
course, it's the software

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.760
on those screens that matters most.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.560
Tesla has its own software.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.210
Its navigation system is built

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.320
with Google Maps data,

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.600
but it's not the Google Maps app.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.433
The media apps,

00:06:04.433 --> 00:06:06.210
like Apple Music and Spotify,

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.050
are built in.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.490
You just sign into your account

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:09.393
on the screen.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:13.467
- Play Fall Out Boy, "We
Didn't Start The Fire."

00:06:15.954 --> 00:06:18.690
- [Joanna V.O.] And you can
pair your phone via Bluetooth.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.390
Ford and Hyundai have
their own software as well,

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.310
which is not as good as Tesla's.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.050
- What is this mess?

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.160
This whole navigation feels like 1995,

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.040
like a MapQuest situation here.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.990
- [Joanna V.O.] But they
also have Android Auto

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.760
and Apple CarPlay.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.776
Specifically, Mustang has...

00:06:37.776 --> 00:06:39.000
- Wireless CarPlay.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.310
No wires, check it out.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.990
- [Joanna V.O.] With the
Apple and Google software,

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.640
you do lose some of that car

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.050
and battery integration,

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.450
which really shines in the Tesla.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.520
- So as soon as you route to a charger,

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.430
it will say "Preconditioning
battery for fast charging."

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.907
The biggest decision I have to make,

00:06:54.907 --> 00:06:57.750
"how badly do I want Apple CarPlay?"

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.110
2023 baby, no wires.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.670
- [Joanna V.O.] So yeah, for this lap...

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.170
- It's a tie,

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.643
Tesla and Ford.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:11.370
- [Joanna V.O.] Lap four,
semi-autonomous driving.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.410
- This is very nerve wracking

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.400
when there's traffic.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.060
Small breaths, trusting
Tesla with my life right now.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.470
- [Joanna V.O.] All these cars have active

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:21.120
driving assistance features,

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.010
which include adaptive cruise control

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.060
and lane centering,

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.650
so the car can control the speed

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.570
and steering on a highway.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:28.403
In the Hyundai,

00:07:28.403 --> 00:07:30.240
using these features requires...

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.790
- Keep hands on steering wheel.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.110
- [Joanna V.O.] But Ford and Tesla have

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.150
more capabilities in this area.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.320
Ford's Blue Cruise prompts you

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.460
to take your hands off

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.690
the wheel on highways.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:40.800
- Oh God, is it gonna do it?

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:42.690
- [Joanna V.O.] Even for lane changes.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.390
You just press on the turn signal and...

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.740
- Okay, it's preparing
for another lane change.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:50.970
Woo hoo!

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.110
All right, it did it, it did it.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.640
Slow down, slow down.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.560
And it slowed down.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.620
- [Joanna V.O.] When you enable
Tesla's enhanced autopilot,

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.970
it does tell you to keep your hands

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.230
on the wheel at first.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.960
But in my tests, it
behaved just like the Ford.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.660
- All right, let's see
if it'll change lanes.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.830
Oh, it's changing lanes.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:08.670
Oh boy, okay.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.970
That is not as smooth as the Ford.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.800
There's just one tiny question

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.570
to ask yourself here.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.530
Which company are you gonna trust

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:17.760
with your life?

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:18.593
- [Joanna V.O.] That is if you can

00:08:18.593 --> 00:08:19.680
actually trust the computer

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.270
to do the driving.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.760
Tesla has additional
self-driving features,

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.380
but I kept taking over the wheel

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.310
when testing them.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.060
- It's gotten off, it's gotten off.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.990
Nope, I got off.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.280
I don't know if it was gonna get off.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.450
I didn't trust it

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.380
and I did it.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.270
- [Joanna V.O.] Overall,
I found Ford's Blue Cruise

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:37.350
easier to figure out

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:38.520
and more informative,

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.720
and that's really what you want

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:40.890
in a situation where

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.990
the computer is your co-pilot.

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.870
- It says "Lane change is
not available right now."

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.703
The Ford wins this round.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.273
- [Joanna V.O.] As much as I like

00:08:50.273 --> 00:08:51.690
the Hyundai's exterior look

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.400
and ultra fast battery charging,

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.440
when I did find a fast charger,

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.360
it wasn't gonna be my next car.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:58.800
But even after that road trip

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.660
and all that track testing,

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.590
I didn't have a decision

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:03.780
between the Ford and the Tesla.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:04.860
Plus, this really did feel

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.630
like a more emotional decision

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.760
than my next laptop or phone.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.650
So I decided to phone, or Zoom,

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.320
a friend who has reviewed
more EVs on YouTube

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.520
than I could count.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.100
- Hey, I'm Marques Brownlee, AKA MKBHD.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.690
- What would you consider

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.980
if you were deciding

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.300
between these two cars?

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.200
- I'm not surprised that

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.460
these are your two final options,

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:24.690
they're both really good.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:25.927
I'd be asking you questions, like,

00:09:25.927 --> 00:09:27.030
"What are you gonna do with it?"

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:30.090
I literally don't recommend non-Tesla EVs

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.070
to people who actually road trip

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.420
with any regularity.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.470
So if that's something you plan

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.349
on doing more than a few times,

00:09:37.349 --> 00:09:39.330
it might be worth it just for that.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.163
- [Joanna V.O.] Given that this is

00:09:40.163 --> 00:09:41.790
a second car for my family,

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.320
I don't expect I'd road trip more

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:44.310
than two to three times

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.750
a year with the EV.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.030
Plus, I'm going to install a home charger,

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.650
and next year Ford will be able

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.600
to use those Tesla chargers.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.400
But Marques was incredibly helpful

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.230
in seeing the bigger picture.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:58.140
- We saw the curve with
phones go like this

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.280
and then sort of even out,

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.240
and now they're mature,

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.160
and they get a little bump every year.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.090
And I think with cars,

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.470
we're right here.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.240
With electric cars,
we're at the beginning.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.680
- So I should lease.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.300
- I leased my first EV

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.950
and I have no regrets about that.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.690
I think in three years,

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:15.630
your computer on wheels
will be much better.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.730
- [Joanna V.O.] And that's
what I've decided to do.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:21.030
Lease a Ford Mustang Mach-E for 36 months,

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.190
and I'll buy a CCS to Tesla adapter

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.540
when it's available.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.580
Because, well, I've always dreamed

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.923
of having a dongle to charge my car.

00:10:34.417 --> 00:10:37.533
- And that's the end of my game show.

